    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The key check is constant-time",
      "items": [
        "Both keys are decoded to bytes before CryptographicOperations.FixedTimeEquals runs",
        "A wrong key takes the same time to reject no matter how much of it happened to be right",
        "A byte-identical key is accepted even if its base64 text differs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "There is no silent re-key",
      "items": [
        "A key mismatch always throws InvalidOperationException",
        "Create a new AesGcmEncryption instance for a different key, or call EncryptString/DecryptString directly",
        "AES-CBC's IAesEncryption, AesEncryption, and AddAesEncryption were removed, with no compatibility shim"
      ]
    }
